Third-party parts

  Built into the program
    DeepFilterNet (libDF) and its DeepFilterNet3 low-latency model, by Hendrik
    Schröter: https://github.com/Rikorose/DeepFilterNet, MIT OR Apache-2.0.
    The model is embedded in the binary unchanged.
    Rust crates (Tauri, serde, tract and others): each under its own license,
    almost all MIT and/or Apache-2.0; a few are MPL-2.0 (cssparser,
    cssparser-macros, dtoa-short, option-ext, selectors), used unchanged from
    crates.io where their source is available. The full list with every
    license text is THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt in each download.

  Shipped beside the program
    ui/fonts: Inter, JetBrains Mono and Noto Sans TC (subsets), SIL Open Font
    License 1.1, see ui/fonts/OFL-*.txt.
    WebView2Loader.dll (Windows): Microsoft Edge WebView2 SDK, redistributable
    under the Microsoft WebView2 SDK license.

  VB-CABLE (Windows download only)
    The Windows download includes the VB-CABLE driver package from VB-Audio
    Software, unchanged. VB-CABLE is not part of stream-mic and is not covered
    by stream-mic's license.
    Origin: www.vb-cable.com
    VB-CABLE is a donationware, all participations are welcome.
    In companies, institutions and public bodies where the people using it
    cannot donate or buy it themselves, VB-Audio asks for paid licenses:
    https://vb-audio.com/Services/licensing.htm

  Not included
    The test and measurement tools (tools/) refer to speech and singing
    corpora (DAPS, VocalSet) that are downloaded separately under their own
    terms; none of their audio is in this repository or the downloads.
